// Copy this file to Config/Local.xcconfig and fill in the two public values.
// Local.xcconfig is gitignored: it is machine-local configuration, never a
// committed secret. These are the same two public values the website uses
// (VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY in .env.local).
//
// Both are public by design. The anon / publishable key grants nothing on its
// own because every table is behind RLS. The service-role key must never appear
// here, in Info.plist, or anywhere else in the app bundle.
//
// Xcode's xcconfig parser treats "//" as the start of a comment, so the "//" in
// a URL is written with the conventional empty-substitution escape: https:/$()/.
// Copy the escape exactly as shown.

SUPABASE_URL = https:/$()/YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = YOUR-ANON-OR-PUBLISHABLE-KEY
